# 144. Binary Tree Preorder Traversal (Iterative Approach)

## APPROACH: BINARY TREE PREORDER TRAVERSAL (ITERATIVE / STACK)

Idea:
Preorder Traversal follow karta hai: Root -> Left -> Right (N-L-R).
Recursion internally call stack use karta hai, yahan hum explicit `Stack` (ya `Deque`) use karke recursion ko simulate karte hain.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Iterative using Stack)

1. Edge Case:
   Agar `root == null` hai, seedha empty list return kar do.

2. Ek Stack (`Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>()`) initialize karo.

3. Sabse pehle `root` ko stack me `push` karo.

4. Jab tak stack empty na ho jaye (`while(!stack.isEmpty())`):
   - Top node ko `pop` karo: `currNode = stack.pop()`.
   - Uski value result list me add karo: `ans.add(currNode.val)`.
   - **Crucial Step (Push Order):**
     1. Pehle `currNode.right` ko stack me push karo (agar null na ho).
     2. Fir `currNode.left` ko stack me push karo (agar null na ho).
   - *(Reason: Stack LIFO follow karta hai, isliye Left child baad me push hoga taaki wo next iteration me pehle pop ho sake).*

5. Loop end hone par `ans` return kar do.

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
      1
     / \
    2   3
   / \
  4   5

Dry Run:
- Initial: Stack = [1], ans = []

Step 1:
- Pop 1 -> ans = [1]
- Push Right (3), Push Left (2)
- Stack = [3, 2] (Top par 2 hai)

Step 2:
- Pop 2 -> ans = [1, 2]
- Push Right (5), Push Left (4)
- Stack = [3, 5, 4] (Top par 4 hai)

Step 3:
- Pop 4 -> ans = [1, 2, 4] (Children null hain)
- Stack = [3, 5]

Step 4:
- Pop 5 -> ans = [1, 2, 4, 5] (Children null hain)
- Stack = [3]

Step 5:
- Pop 3 -> ans = [1, 2, 4, 5, 3] (Children null hain)
- Stack empty

Result: [1, 2, 4, 5, 3]

--------------------------------------------------

WHY STACK & WHY PUSH RIGHT FIRST?

- Stack LIFO (Last In, First Out) order maintain karta hai.
- Preorder me Left ko Right se pehle process karna hota hai.
- Isliye hum intentionally Right child ko pehle stack ke bottom me bhejte hain, taaki Left child stack ke top par rahe aur pehle process ho.

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
H = Height of binary tree

Time:
O(N) -> Har node exactly ek baar stack me push aur pop hoti hai.

Space:
O(H) -> Stack me at any point at most tree ki height ke proportional nodes rahenge.
Worst case (skewed tree): O(N)
Best/Average case (balanced tree): O(log N)
*(Excluding output list ans)*

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

- Stack selection: Java me `Stack` class legacy aur synchronized (slow) hoti hai, isliye modern code me hamesha `ArrayDeque` prefer karte hain: `Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>()`.
- Interviewer ka classic trap: "Tumne pehle right push kiya ya left?" -> Reason clearly explain karna ki stack LIFO hone ki wajah se Right pehle push hota hai taaki Left pehle bahar nikle.
- Follow-up: *"Can you do traversal in O(1) space?"* -> Yes, Morris Traversal (Threaded Binary Tree concept).

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

import java.util.*;

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> preorderTraversal(TreeNode root) {
        List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        helper(ans, root);
        return ans;
    }

    private void helper(List<Integer> ans, TreeNode root) {
        if (root == null) {
            return;
        }

        Deque<TreeNode> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();
        stack.push(root);

        while (!stack.isEmpty()) {
            TreeNode currNode = stack.pop();
            ans.add(currNode.val);

            // Right child pehle push hoga
            if (currNode.right != null) {
                stack.push(currNode.right);
            }
            // Left child baad me push hoga taaki pehle pop ho
            if (currNode.left != null) {
                stack.push(currNode.left);
            }
        }
    }
}
